# --- Koch (16703338)
("16703338", "curious", 1, "Koch's postulates were formulated in the late nineteenth century as guidelines for establishing that microbes cause specific diseases",
 ("What are Koch's postulates for?", ["Classifying antibiotics by their mechanism", "Establishing that a microbe causes a disease", "Measuring the strength of an immune response", "Naming new bacterial species formally"],
  "Koch's postulates are criteria to link a specific microbe to a specific disease; prions and viruses challenged them.", "Microbe → disease causation."),
 ("¿Para qué sirven los postulados de Koch?", ["Clasificar antibióticos según su mecanismo", "Establecer que un microbio causa una enfermedad", "Medir la intensidad de una respuesta inmune", "Nombrar formalmente nuevas especies bacterianas"],
  "Los postulados de Koch son criterios para vincular un microbio con una enfermedad; los priones y virus los pusieron a prueba.", "Causalidad microbio → enfermedad.")),
("16703338", "researcher", 2, "their applicability to inanimate pathogens such as viruses and infectious proteins has been problematic",
 ("Why are Koch's original postulates hard to apply to viruses and prions?", ["They are too small to stain with dyes", "They infect only plant and insect cells", "They were designed for culturable bacteria", "They never produce consistent disease"],
  "The postulates assume culturable living agents; viruses and infectious proteins don't fit easily.", "Designed for culturable bacteria."),
 ("¿Por qué los postulados originales de Koch son difíciles de aplicar a virus y priones?", ["Son demasiado pequeños para teñirlos", "Solo infectan células de plantas e insectos", "Se diseñaron para bacterias cultivables", "Nunca producen una enfermedad constante"],
  "Los postulados suponen agentes vivos cultivables; los virus y las proteínas infecciosas no encajan fácilmente.", "Pensados para bacterias cultivables.")),

